---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const snippet =
  '<iframe src="https://visafreely.com/embed/" title="Visa requirements checker by VisaFreely" width="100%" height="430" style="border:0;width:100%;max-width:560px" loading="lazy"></iframe>';
---

<Base
  title="Free Visa Checker Widget for Travel Blogs — visafreely"
  description="Embed visafreely's visa-requirements checker on your blog or travel site for free: one iframe, no signup, always-current data with verified dates."
>
  <h1>Put the visa checker on your site</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Writing about a route your readers keep asking visa questions about? Drop this checker into the
    post and they can look the answer up without leaving your page. It is free, needs no signup or
    API key, and it runs on the same data as this site — including the “last verified” dates, so it
    never goes stale when a rule changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>This is the widget itself, live:</p>
  <iframe
    class="widget-demo"
    src="/embed/?p=JP&d=TH"
    title="Visa requirements checker by VisaFreely — live demo"
    loading="lazy"></iframe>

  <h2>Add it to your site</h2>
  <p>
    Copy this snippet and paste it into any HTML page or blog post where you want the checker to
    appear:
  </p>
  <div class="snippet-box">
    <textarea id="widget-snippet" readonly rows="4" spellcheck="false">{snippet}</textarea>
    <button type="button" class="copy-btn" id="widget-copy">Copy snippet</button>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">
    The frame is 560px wide at most and 430px tall; it shrinks to fit narrow screens. On WordPress
    it goes in a “Custom HTML” block, on other platforms in any HTML/embed field.
  </p>

  <h2>Good to know</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:20px;">
      <li>
        <strong>Always current.</strong> The widget reads the live visafreely index — the same one
        behind the checker on our home page. Corrections and new verifications show up automatically;
        there is nothing to update on your side.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Honest answers.</strong> Each result shows the requirement, the maximum stay, and
        either the date the pair was last verified against an official source or a plain note that
        the value comes from the dataset and is not yet individually verified.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pre-select a route.</strong> Writing about one specific trip? Add
        <code>?p=JP&amp;d=TH</code> to the embed address (two-letter country codes) and the widget
        opens with that route already answered — the demo above does exactly this.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The full page is one tap away.</strong> Every result links to the pair's full
        requirement page here, with the requirement details, official source and related routes.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p>
    Questions about the data behind it? See <a href="/about/">how verification works</a>.
  </p>

  <style>
    .widget-demo {
      border: 0;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 560px;
      height: 430px;
      display: block;
      background: transparent;
    }
    .snippet-box {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin: 12px 0 6px;
    }
    .snippet-box textarea {
      flex: 1 1 420px;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      color: var(--ink);
      background: var(--soft);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      resize: vertical;
    }
    .copy-btn {
      background: var(--brand);
      color: #fff;
      font: inherit;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 14.5px;
      padding: 10px 18px;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 999px;
      cursor: pointer;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .copy-btn:hover { background: var(--brand-deep); }
  </style>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var btn = document.getElementById('widget-copy');
      var box = document.getElementById('widget-snippet');
      if (!btn || !box) return;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        function done() {
          btn.textContent = 'Copied ✓';
          setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = 'Copy snippet'; }, 2000);
        }
        if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(box.value).then(done, function () {
            box.select();
            document.execCommand('copy');
            done();
          });
        } else {
          box.select();
          document.execCommand('copy');
          done();
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
